\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let E $g(x)=integral_S2$ g(omega) exp(2pi i x dot omega) d sigma(omega). For every $p>3$, is there $C_p$ with ||E $g||_Lp(R3)<=C_p||g||_Linfinity(S2)$ for all bounded measurable g?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let E $g(x)=integral_S2$ g(omega) exp(2pi i x dot omega) d sigma(omega). For every $p>3$, is there $C_p$ with ||E $g||_Lp(R3)<=C_p||g||_Linfinity(S2)$ for all bounded measurable g?

